# The most a compute entry point may hold, compiled alone as the build compiles its module: its SPIR-V's bytes, its
# local arrays and their bytes a thread (tools/nocontract/budget.hpp). The test spirv_budget holds each to its own line,
# else to the line "*" (cmake/Shaders.cmake); a stage that would pass it is split instead, as the windows' decide
# stages are (shaders/building/draw.slang).
#
# <module>:<entry point>  <bytes>  <local arrays>  <their bytes>
#
# Every compute entry point: alpha 15's windows_cs (7e44abe), the last windows' decide stage the user's PowerVR phone
# ran. From alpha 16 the map froze there at about z 17, the first frame that ran it, once it had grown to 333,400 bytes
# with 53 local arrays of 5,088 bytes a thread over the same walls (the audit of 28 October 2026).
*  211280  17  780
# Stages alpha 15 already shipped larger, unchanged since, which the phone ran: held at their alpha 15 bytes until they
# are split under the line above.
item_draw:items_cs  418600  17  780
tree_draw:things_cs  234116  17  780
